Harmattan: video frames from gltexturesink without a copy

QVideoSurfaceGstSink copied every DSP-decoded frame into a texture: video took 100% CPU and
wasn't smooth. With GStreamer 0.10, QGstreamerVideoRenderer now uses Nokia's gltexturesink in
video-texture mode (Qt Quick's EGL display and context) when the surface takes its frames,
and the new harmattan videonode plugin binds each one (EGL images, GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES)
and releases it behind a fence, as Qt Mobility's QGstreamerGLTextureRenderer did. Elsewhere,
or before VideoOutput has an OpenGL context, the copying sink stays.

